And "frame.anchors 在文档内链接跳转中起到什么作用":
- frame.anchors is an `EcoVec<(Point, EcoString)>` - pairs of positions (Point in frame coordinates) and IDs.
- It's populated by `traverse_frame` in link.rs when a link target is located INSIDE an html.frame. For each link target inside the frame, traverse_frame computes the frame-internal position (via the introspector's HtmlPosition details) and pushes `(point, id)` to anchors.
- In svg_in_html, each anchor is rendered via `render_anchor(&mut svg, *pos, id)` - this creates an invisible linkable `<a>` element (or anchor point) inside the SVG at that position with that ID.
- This allows document-internal links (and cross-document bundle links) to jump to a precise point inside the SVG-embedded content, preserving the introspection/linking system even when content is rasterized to SVG.

